# Declared intentional — craft findings kept on purpose, with the reason.
# Format: <finding-id>  <why>
#
# Per §24 of the capability map, a declared finding is not suppressed. It moves
# to a separate list in the report, because the declaration is the artifact
# worth keeping — whether the writer knew is a better signal than whether the
# line follows the rule.

SING:CHORUS:S0:L2:hands       "Hands cold" is the hook. The cluster is the grit and it sits on a short note, not a held one.
SING:CHORUS#2:S0:L2:hands     Same line, second chorus. Deliberate.
SING:CHORUS-(out):S0:L2:hands Same line, last chorus. Deliberate.
SING:BRIDGE:S0:L0:months      "Nine months" is the whole bridge. /nths/ is hard and the difficulty is the point — it should sound like effort.
SING:BRIDGE:S0:L1:months      Repeated on purpose; see above.
SING:VERSE-2:S0:L2:hazards    Kept. "Hazards on" is the image the verse is built around and no synonym carries it.
